review:
Absolute cinema.

A lot of the negative reviews of this game, as harsh is this is going to sound, is literally just skill issues. Don't feel dissuaded. This game is MEANT to be hard. I played this as my very first Resident Evil game EVER - never touched RE, never had the story spoiled, nothing - and I played it on Normal difficulty within 18 hours. If I can do it despite having never touched controls of this nature, then anyone can do it.

If you enter this game knowing it'll be hard,
if you enter this game knowing it's meant to make you THINK and think HARD,
if you enter this game knowing it's going to kick your ass mercilessly,
if you enter this game knowing it expects you to be open minded,
.. then you'll love it.

Also, don't download the damn item box mod. Seriously, you're killing half the point.

Even though it was released after the first Resident Evil (2002) remake, this game still misses almost every core concept of the original Resident Evil trilogy.

TLDR:

IF you are an old timer RE fan (original trilogy fan specially) OR are on a trip to play all RE games OR just wanna play it and give it a taste:
 > do it, although I would recommend NORMAL or EASY difficulties as anything harder than that may get very frustrating.

ELSE:
> just don't; the game is mediocre at best and there are other RE games that would suit better for both original or new RE enjoyers or even newcomers.

[hr][/hr]
[olist]
[*] doesn't add anything relevant to the plot;
[*] poor design for enemies;
[*] enemies have few to none damage feedback. When an enemy is bound to hit you, most of the time, hitting it mid attack animation won't prevent the monster from hitting/grabbing you;
[*] enemies may camp doors (as a side effect of the interchangeable character mechanics) and insta grab you the moment you enter the room/area;
[*] tough enemies may need a bunch shots to get dispatched;
[*] the possibility of exchanging items is cool at first but gets really clunky as you progress;
[*] some game mechanics get very inefficient due to menu/dialogue navigation speed. e.g., the item elevator thingy;
[*] some quick enemies also hit using a minimum amount of frames, with no balance between movement and attack speed whatsoever: the moment they reach you, the insta hit you, no escape;
[*] enemies may stun lock you to death with quick hits. e.g., [spoiler]monkeys as they are usually found in packs of 2 or more[/spoiler];
[*] triggering some game events disable one of the two characters and then you are expected manage the situation with the remaining one. e.g., [spoiler]the centipede (boss fight) grabs rebecca, so you have to fight and save her using billy, what means if you have your main equipment placed on rebecca's inventory, you are screwed as you can't use those items. so in that specific case if your spare equipment is not enough or you don't have the ability of foresight, you are expected to die, reset, exchange equipment and try again[/spoiler];
[*] in hard difficulty, some sections may get very frustrating sometimes, as enemies get huge amounts of HP and become virtually damage sponges;
[*] poor design for boss fights. e.g., [spoiler]the queen leech fight mimics the original Resident Evil 3: Nemesis final boss fight gimmick to a point even the creature design is similar[/spoiler];
[/olist]

Resident Evil 0
cons:
//difficult movement controls and awful spectator camera angles
//lack of directions
//requires youtube walkthrough or most likely get lost
//overexcessive backtracking gameplay
//awful inventory management
//requires micromanagement puzzle solving between two characters

//sucks

// H // O // T :::: // R // U // N //
// R // E // V // I // E // W // S //

Inventory management hell & constant backtracking. You will lose your progress often and your sanity if you play more than 2 hrs. Play Resident Evil 1-4 and The Evil Within 1 and 2 instead. Time to uninstall.

If you enjoy the franchise then why not give this one a try? It has its moments and the atmosphere is quite good too. 

PRO: 
-fun to play; 
-story is ok and puts in some missing pieces of the whole resident evil universe; 
-tons of costume; 
-puzzles are on the easy side


CON: 
-if you finished the game in 5 hours then you probably spent 3 hrs organising the inventory and/or running back and forth to collect items you 'dropped' on the floor...
-enemies at higher difficulties can be tricky to dispatch with limited resources
